00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:46,000
1,000,000 tons. 100,000 lives. 100 minutes.

2
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:26,000
Unstoppable is a action, thriller film directed by Tony Scott.

3
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:06,000
When a massive, unmanned locomotive roars out of control, the
threat is more ominous than just a derailment.

4
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:46,000
The train is laden with toxic chemicals, and an accident would
decimate human life and cause an environmental disaster.

5
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:26,000
The only hope of bringing the train to a safe stop is in the hands of veteran engineer Frank Barnes, and
young conductor Will Colson, who must risk their lives to save those in the runaway's path.

6
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Inspired by true events.

7
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:46,000
Frank Barnes, played by Denzel Washington.

8
00:37:20,000 --> 00:37:26,000
Will Colson, played by Chris Pine.

9
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
Connie Hooper, played by Rosario Dawson.

10
00:46:40,000 --> 00:46:46,000
Oscar Galvin, VP of Operations, played by Kevin Dunn.

11
00:51:20,000 --> 00:51:26,000
Inspector Scott Werner, played by Kevin Corrigan.

12
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
Ned Oldham, played by Lew Temple.

13
01:00:40,000 --> 01:00:46,000
Unstoppable is a 2010 American disaster thriller film directed and produced by Tony Scott,
written by Mark Bomback, and starring Denzel Washington and Chris Pine.

14
01:05:20,000 --> 01:05:26,000
It is based on the real-life CSX 8888 incident, telling the story of a
runaway freight train and the two men who attempt to stop it.

15
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
It was the last film Scott directed before his death in 2012.

16
01:14:40,000 --> 01:14:46,000
The film was released in the United States on
November 12, 2010, by 20th Century Fox.

17
01:19:20,000 --> 01:19:26,000
It received generally positive reviews from critics and grossed $167.8
million against a production budget between $85–100 million.

18
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
It was nominated for an Oscar for Best Sound Editing at the 83rd Academy Awards, and for Best Action
Movie at the 2011 Critics' Choice Movie Awards, but lost to Inception in both cases.

19
01:28:40,000 --> 01:28:46,000
The film explores themes of pennsylvania, usa, locomotive,
freight train, evacuation, based on true story.

